<title>PHILIPPINES: BPI eyes stake in insurance brokerage firm.</title>
<headline>BPI eyes stake in insurance brokerage firm.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of the Philippine Islands (BPI) said on Friday its executive committee had approved in principle a 33.33 percent investment plan in a local insurance brokerage firm.</p>
<p>The bank told the Philippine Stock Exchange that BPI planned to invest in Ayala Bain Insurance Brokerages Inc, a joint venture between its parent Ayala Corp and AON-Bain Hogg Group of the United Kingdom.</p>
<p>The bank did not say how much the investment would cost.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
